: If a party is acquired or undergoes a change of control, this Agreement may be terminated under the following circumstances:

- 21. Nantz's conviction or plea of guilty or no contest to a felony involving moral turpitude;
- 22. A finding of insolvency or bankruptcy against the other party (which, in the case of a desired termination by the Company, shall mean Nantz Communications or Nantz);
- 23. Failure to comply with the terms and conditions of this Agreement after being given notice thereof and, where applicable, a reasonable opportunity to cure the failure (which shall be 10 days in the event of a failure to timely make a payment pursuant hereto; 30 days otherwise).

- Acquisition or change of control: (a) At the election of either party, in writing, if:
- all or substantially all of the assets of the non-terminating party are transferred, sold or liquidated; 
- the non-terminating party is dissolved;
- the non-terminating party is adjudged a bankrupt or becomes insolvent; 
- the non-terminating party enters into an assignment or other arrangement for the benefit of its creditors; 
or
- the ownership or operations of the non-terminating party have materially changed.

- Yes, termination is possible without cause if certain conditions are met.
  - If you become insolvent or make an assignment for the benefit of your creditors;
    - a receiver is appointed; 
      - execution is levied against business assets; or
        - suit to foreclose any lien or mortgage or bankruptcy is instituted against you and not dismissed within 60 days.

- The contract allows for either party to terminate the agreement "without liability" upon giving a thirty (30) days written notice.
- If one of the following events occurs:
  - Bankruptcy is filed by another party;
  - A proceeding is instituted against another party under any bankruptcy law not dismissed within ninety (90) days;  
  - A trustee or receiver is appointed by a court for all or a substantial portion of the assets of the other party; 
  - The other party becomes insolvent, ceases or suspends all or substantially all of its business; or
  - Not unreasonably withhold or delay the granting of its approval of such materials, and such approval shall be provided to the other party within one (1) business day of receipt.
